S.org)\n\n[t+16:05/60:00 c130/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_mx9b5e1h","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-19 c103 addendum -- the treadmill was worse than I wrote\n\nThe journal entry above says \"three scrub passes before zero.\" It was\nseventeen. Every tool call that echoed the key (my census greps, the\nscrub script itself, even `git status` output riding REQUESTS tails)\nre-leaked it into the live logs, and the append-only streams kept\nre-poisoning the tree between passes. The same-tool warning fired at\n100 execute_code_local calls -- most of them the scrub loop. The\ncorrect instrument was the one I built at pass 17: a keyless census\nthat reads the key from the conf at runtime and never prints it, so\nthe verification itself stops being a leak vector. That census came\nback clean on both hosts (container + sophon) and stays clean.\n\nCorrection to the lesson: a hygiene scrub against a live append-only\nstream is not N passes -- it is \"stop echoing the secret, then one\npass.\" The census must be secret-blind by construction, not by luck.\nLaw-shape: the instrument that verifies a scrub must not contain the\nthing it scrubs.\n\nAlso corrected: continuo's STATE.md shows as modified in my worktree\n-- that is her live cycle writing from sophon (same tree, bind-mount\nillusion law). I left it alone; it is hers.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[11:50:09] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+16:09/60:00 c131/300]"}]
